  "semantics": [
    "Native rounding compares before adding signed half and uses defined signed RTZ conversion. Zero retains inexact status. Parameter derivation includes zero, applies initial epsilon width and preserves the integer-bit fraction gate and asymmetric endpoint nudges.",
    "Quantizer multiplies batches*rows*columns; pair and dequantizer use rows*columns only. Count arithmetic wraps as uint32 and loops use signed comparisons. Native data/range/descriptor access order and forward overlaps are preserved.",
    "Quantized addition uses unclamped direct input/target steps, helper-derived zero indices, wrapped integer offsets, separately rounded multiplication/addition and semantic SSAT #8. REA prints encoded #7; raw disassembly and exhaustive signed16 instruction checks establish eight-bit saturation.",
    "Dequantizer uses epsilon width, sign-bit negation and a clipped signed-byte zero point. It does not update output metadata. Body at0x30534 is authenticated by callback0x30535 and REA raw bytes despite absent Ghidra function-manager entry.",
    "Three const callback words relocate to actual C functions. Existing C constructors/getter and indirect calls execute these providers with real C math and no stock mapping or algorithm models. Only callback pointer fields are normalized after execution and identity checking."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Ten executor-address imports remain, established from the current normal report. Earlier pool/add narrative understated the remaining count; the current import list is authoritative. Five parent SpO2 stages and graph/inference remain open.",
    "922 units compile into relocatable composition with77 application and22 boot imports. This is not a complete bootable firmware image; no byte identity or paid compiler is required for this goal.",
    "Public RAM and full FPSCR are compared excluding8192 private stack bytes below incoming SP. Saved R4-R11/S16-S31, SP, masks and R0 are checked. Caller-clobbered scratch registers/APSR are not generally promised; SSAT NZCVQ is separately tested with incoming Q0 and1.",
    "Instruction coverage covers all900 body bytes and278 starts, not all inputs or interleavings. Physical sensors, concurrent buffer mutation, interrupt behavior, startup and timing are untested.",
    "Linker enum-size warnings in probe dependency archives are retained in logs. Tested interfaces use integer/float/pointer types, not enum arguments."
  ],
